{
  "_comment": [
    "sg13g2-bandgap -- `klt sim` request template for startup-trip-point-pex",
    "(issue #387). Same grid and measurements as the legacy run_pvt_sweep.sh",
    "loop; instantiated by run_klt_sim.sh through sim/harness/pex_runner.sh.",
    "",
    "WHY PER-SUPPLY. The dc sweep's stop value and two measurement levels scale",
    "with the supply: the legacy loop sweeps Vsns1 0..VDD (step 5 mV), measures",
    "the trip point at v(det) = VDD/2 and the 'core fully up' end state one step",
    "short of VDD (ngspice refuses `.meas at=` at the exact end of a dc sweep).",
    "The runner substitutes @@VDD@@, @@VDD_HALF@@ (%.4f of VDD/2) and",
    "@@VDD_OFF@@ (%.4f of VDD-0.05) exactly as the legacy awk did, and pins",
    "`corners.supply_v` to that supply, one request per (process, supply).",
    "",
    "The legacy `op` before the sweep (cold-start state, sns1 = 0) is the first",
    "point of the dc sweep: det_on_v / fb_on_v are measured `at=0`.",
    "",
    "The six-criteria pass/fail verdict is not expressible as a limit on one",
    "measurement; sim/harness/cmos5l_klt.py enrich --kind trip-point re-grades",
    "each point with sim/lib/pvt_verdict_common.sh's formula (kind-generic; it",
    "carries no CMOS5L-specific logic)."
  ],
  "engine": "ngspice",
  "netlist": "@@BODY@@",
  "netlist_source": "extracted",
  "models": { "lib": "@@CORNER_BUNDLE@@" },
  "corners": {
    "process": ["typ", "bcs", "wcs", "sf", "fs"],
    "supply_v": { "Vvdd": [2.97, 3.3, 3.63] },
    "temperature_c": [-40, 27, 125]
  },
  "analysis": { "kind": "dc", "args": "Vsns1 0 @@VDD@@ 0.005" },
  "measurements": [
    { "name": "det_on_v", "spice": ".meas dc det_on_v find v(det) at=0" },
    { "name": "fb_on_v", "spice": ".meas dc fb_on_v find v(fb) at=0" },
    { "name": "vtrip_v", "spice": ".meas dc vtrip_v when v(det)=@@VDD_HALF@@ cross=1" },
    { "name": "det_off_v", "spice": ".meas dc det_off_v find v(det) at=@@VDD_OFF@@" },
    { "name": "fb_off_v", "spice": ".meas dc fb_off_v find v(fb) at=@@VDD_OFF@@" }
  ],
  "options": {
    "timeout_s": 300,
    "keep_artifacts": true
  }
}
